  "title": "Composing knots like cycles reduces to rectangular knots, not to a difference operation",
  "subject": "Converse of the difference-law characterization of circuit elimination",
  "conclusion": "Composing knots like cycles does not force a difference operation: parity beside an unrelated law does it without one. The converse reduces exactly to rectangularity of knots, since rectangular knots compose like cycles precisely when no two meeting at a variable split its range; this is proved on two values, and every tested three-variable knot on up to four values supports it.",
